WEBVTT

00:00:03.778 --> 00:00:06.926
Equity work rarely begins with a framework.

00:00:07.048 --> 00:00:14.963
It begins with a notice that confuses people, a policy choice that
is still open, or a team conversation you want to handle well.

00:00:15.086 --> 00:00:19.514
How the program works starts from that reality by asking what you
are working on.

00:00:19.637 --> 00:00:26.527
You can choose Build your understanding to explore knowledge and
examples, Work through a decision to examine who is affected and

00:00:26.527 --> 00:00:32.381
compare options, or Understand what helped to look beyond what was
completed to what changed for people.

00:00:32.948 --> 00:00:39.093
If you would rather begin with an example, the next section offers
situations that may feel familiar.

00:00:39.216 --> 00:00:46.494
In one, a disability service team wants to clarify a notice about a
service change, knowing that a shorter letter will not help if

00:00:46.494 --> 00:00:49.649
people cannot tell what it means for their support.

00:00:49.771 --> 00:00:56.977
Each example shows what you could take back and how you would know
more, by asking people to explain their next step rather than

00:00:56.977 --> 00:00:58.516
counting letters sent.

00:00:59.082 --> 00:01:04.093
At the center of the page are five connected areas, each built
around a question.

00:01:04.216 --> 00:01:10.381
What informs our work brings together policy, evidence, staff
knowledge and community perspectives.

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:18.714
Put equity into practice asks what we do with what we know, and
helps you choose an activity that fits a real question or decision.

00:01:18.837 --> 00:01:25.088
Tools and resources asks what we can use or produce, such as a
course or a draft analysis.

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:29.479
Explore them in any order and return as your work develops.

00:01:30.046 --> 00:01:33.279
The last two areas look past the activity itself.

00:01:33.401 --> 00:01:41.032
Review progress asks what changed in practice and how people
experienced it, using observations and feedback rather than ratings

00:01:41.032 --> 00:01:42.524
of individual staff.

00:01:42.647 --> 00:01:52.551
Lasting change asks what should improve over time, such as access to
opportunity, workplace participation, service experiences and trust.

00:01:52.673 --> 00:01:55.907
Those changes require evidence over time.

00:01:56.029 --> 00:02:04.130
The page adds a reminder: a prepared document does not establish
approval or implementation, so identify the people affected and the

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:06.640
office responsible for the decision.

00:02:07.207 --> 00:02:11.102
How this program operates shows what holds the pieces together.

00:02:11.224 --> 00:02:19.074
The Program charter connects the purpose, operating principles,
consultant responsibilities, authority boundaries and evidence

00:02:19.074 --> 00:02:21.181
needed to carry work forward.

00:02:21.303 --> 00:02:28.805
The requirements and review evidence workspace helps you identify
applicable requirements, connect them with sources and prepare

00:02:28.805 --> 00:02:31.332
evidence for the responsible reviewer.

00:02:31.454 --> 00:02:38.980
Where a step from the Aging and Disability Services Administration
plan applies, the six-goal implementation map links it to practical

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:39.561
work.

00:02:39.683 --> 00:02:43.894
Those twenty-eight steps do not limit the program's broader equity
work.

00:02:44.461 --> 00:02:52.960
Further down, the page explains operationalizing equity: moving it
out of awareness training and slogans and into how the organization

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:56.494
decides, spends, hires, serves and corrects itself.

00:02:56.617 --> 00:03:04.720
Equity lives inside real decisions, not beside them, which means
policies, budgets, forms and services get an equity look while they

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:06.063
can still change.

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:09.377
It is everyone's work with named owners.

00:03:09.499 --> 00:03:17.050
Progress is measured at the program level, never by scoring or
surveilling individuals, and no single tool becomes a personnel

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:17.710
label.

00:03:18.277 --> 00:03:22.287
The program rests on three pillars that work as a cycle.

00:03:22.409 --> 00:03:30.115
Engagement surfaces what staff and communities experience, analysis
turns that into evidence about the system, and applied practice

00:03:30.115 --> 00:03:33.357
changes a specific decision with a specific owner.

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:37.817
The first pillar treats staff as participants, not audiences.

00:03:37.939 --> 00:03:45.420
Engagement is voluntary, private and non-shaming, so you can learn
on your own time and reflect without being recorded.

00:03:45.542 --> 00:03:52.191
Feedback loops close, which means staff hear what changed because of
their input, and what could not change and why.

00:03:52.758 --> 00:03:56.927
The second pillar is about seeing the pattern, not the person.

00:03:57.049 --> 00:04:05.177
You follow the data by community, language, disability and place,
say plainly what the data does not show, and look at each decision

00:04:05.177 --> 00:04:08.371
point to ask who is delayed, denied or missing.

00:04:08.493 --> 00:04:16.172
Individual conduct belongs in a confidential Human Resources
channel; a systemic pattern belongs in equity practice.

00:04:16.294 --> 00:04:20.772
The third pillar, applied practices, fixes the system where it
lives.

00:04:20.894 --> 00:04:29.407
Every analysis ends with something usable, with a named owner and a
review date, built into documents the organization already uses.

00:04:29.973 --> 00:04:34.089
The page closes with six commitments behind every decision.

00:04:34.211 --> 00:04:36.742
Equity is everyone's work.

00:04:36.864 --> 00:04:39.391
Build on existing infrastructure.

00:04:39.513 --> 00:04:41.741
Center lived experience.

00:04:41.863 --> 00:04:43.497
Follow the data.

00:04:43.619 --> 00:04:45.786
Move at the speed of trust.

00:04:45.908 --> 00:04:48.094
Work in partnership.

00:04:48.217 --> 00:04:53.850
Together, they describe a program that respects your expertise and
the people you serve.

00:04:53.972 --> 00:05:01.255
When you are ready, return to the top of the page, choose the
starting point that matches what you are working on today, and take

00:05:01.255 --> 00:05:02.967
one small, concrete step.
